{
	title: "Claude's own web_search tool",
	spec: 'Requests to Anthropic Claude models include Anthropic\'s server-side web_search tool (type web_search_20250305 or the newest, max_uses 5), so Claude searches the web itself; other providers do not get it and use the google tool (task g6). The stream\'s server_tool_use and web_search_tool_result blocks are kept in history as provider-specific blocks and replayed only to Anthropic, in order and paired: an unpaired one (an interrupted turn, a compaction boundary) is dropped on replay so the API never sees half a pair. Clients show a search as a tool row: "web_search <query>" with the result titles and URLs; its cost counts in usage. A setting webSearch (config.ason, default true) turns it off. Artifact: the old Hal anthropic.ts web_search handling (reference, tasks/9m/old-anthropic-web-search.ts). Tests with the fake Anthropic server: the tool is offered to Claude only; paired blocks replay; an orphan is dropped; the setting turns it off.',
	status: 'planned',
	needs: ['ya']
}
